.TH TAR 1 "February 2026" "Substrate" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tar \- create, list, append, update, and extract tar archives
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tar
.B -cxtur
.RB [ -v ]
.RB [ -f " archive" ]
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ files ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tar
implements a POSIX-style archiver with ustar and PAX support.
The default output format is PAX to preserve long paths and large numeric metadata.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -c
Create an archive.
.TP
.BR -x
Extract an archive.
.TP
.BR -t
List archive contents.
.TP
.BR -r , " --concatenate"
Append files to an existing regular-file archive.
.TP
.BR -u
Update archive with files changed since the existing archive/snapshot state.
.TP
.BR -f " file"
Use archive
.IR file .
Use
.B -
for standard input/output.
.TP
.BR --format=ustar | pax
Choose archive format.
.TP
.BR -z , " --gzip"
Use external
.B gzip
for compression/decompression.
.TP
.BR -J , " --xz"
Use external
.B xz
for compression/decompression.
.TP
.BR -j , " --bzip2"
Use external
.B bzip2
for compression/decompression.
.TP
.BR --safe-extract
Reject archive entries that are absolute or contain parent traversal components.
.TP
.BR --strip-components = N
Strip the first
.I N
path components while extracting.
.TP
.BR --no-overwrite
Do not overwrite existing files while extracting.
.TP
.BR --no-same-owner
Do not restore archived ownership.
.TP
.BR --preserve-permissions
Restore archived permissions.
.TP
.BR --keep-directory-symlink
Fail when extracting through symlinked parent directories.
.TP
.BR --listed-incremental = SNAP
Enable snapshot-based incremental creation/update.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error or archive processing error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Create archive:
.PP
.EX
tar -cf src.tar src/
.EE
.PP
Extract safely:
.PP
.EX
tar -xf src.tar --safe-extract --strip-components=1
.EE
.PP
Incremental backup:
.PP
.EX
tar -cf backup.tar --listed-incremental=.snap project/
tar -uf backup.tar --listed-incremental=.snap project/
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pax (1),
.BR cpio (1)
